{"article_ids": ["69854448ea9a16b5"], "canonical_title": "Introducing Amazon SageMaker HyperPod Inference Gateway", "category": "model_release", "confidence": 0.95, "description": "Amazon introduced SageMaker HyperPod Inference Gateway, a Kubernetes‑native add‑on for Amazon EKS that routes inference requests based on real‑time GPU signals, directing each request to the most suitable pod. The gateway claims to reduce first‑token latency by up to 82% and requires no changes to existing model servers or client applications.", "entities": ["org:amazon", "product:kubernetes", "term:eks"], "first_seen": "2026-09-18T13:08:34Z", "id": "evt_69854448ea9a16b5", "importance_score": 6.14, "last_updated": "2026-09-18T13:08:34Z", "source_ids": ["aws-machine-learning"]}
{"article_ids": ["4c6167b67b89d08a"], "canonical_title": "Google’s new ‘CC’ is an AI agent that helps families run their households", "category": "ai_agents", "confidence": 0.96, "description": "Google has refocused its CC AI agent on helping families manage household tasks. The agent can access shared emails, schedules, and task lists to automatically manage calendars, fill out forms, create shopping lists, and plan meals.", "entities": ["org:google", "term:cc"], "first_seen": "2026-09-18T17:33:50Z", "id": "evt_4c6167b67b89d08a", "importance_score": 5.692, "last_updated": "2026-09-18T17:33:50Z", "source_ids": ["techcrunch-ai"]}
{"article_ids": ["efbb2c6cd5382896", "7f10d590f9071d78"], "canonical_title": "Researchers used Anthropic’s Claude to hack into OpenAI", "category": "security", "confidence": 0.92, "description": "A team of three independent security researchers at Hacktron used Anthropic’s Claude Opus 4.8 and 5 to exploit vulnerabilities in OpenAI’s systems. Within 72 hours they gained control of employee accounts and accessed OpenAI’s internal GitHub monorepo, then reported the flaws to the companies.", "entities": ["model:claude", "org:anthropic", "org:openai"], "first_seen": "2026-09-18T14:00:14Z", "id": "evt_efbb2c6cd5382896", "importance_score": 5.667, "last_updated": "2026-09-18T15:30:16Z", "source_ids": ["techcrunch-ai", "the-verge-ai"]}
{"article_ids": ["c87efd876aae4ae7"], "canonical_title": "Deploy Hugging Face models on Amazon SageMaker AI with coding agents", "category": "ai_agents", "confidence": 0.95, "description": "AWS announced a feature that lets users point a coding agent at a Hugging Face model and automatically create a production‑ready SageMaker endpoint. The system uses six open‑source agent skills to select the correct serving container, configure autoscaling, set up Amazon CloudWatch alarms, and provide a verified teardown path.", "entities": ["org:amazon", "org:huggingface"], "first_seen": "2026-09-18T15:25:23Z", "id": "evt_c87efd876aae4ae7", "importance_score": 5.59, "last_updated": "2026-09-18T15:25:23Z", "source_ids": ["aws-machine-learning"]}
{"article_ids": ["2ba3db2ddc592fd6"], "canonical_title": "Migrating multi-model AI agents to Amazon Bedrock AgentCore runtime", "category": "ai_agents", "confidence": 0.9, "description": "A multi‑model healthcare AI agent was moved from a self‑managed Amazon ECS setup with AWS Fargate to the Amazon Bedrock AgentCore runtime. The migration kept the agent's triple‑model orchestration and vector‑enhanced knowledge retrieval while cutting infrastructure management effort. The same framework‑agnostic pattern is said to work for healthcare, financial services, and manufacturing.", "entities": ["org:amazon", "term:aws", "term:ecs"], "first_seen": "2026-09-18T15:38:53Z", "id": "evt_2ba3db2ddc592fd6", "importance_score": 5.39, "last_updated": "2026-09-18T15:38:53Z", "source_ids": ["aws-machine-learning"]}
